{
  "timestamp": "2026-07-27T15:33:55Z",
  "title": "Login opcional con Apple y Google",
  "type": "feature",
  "userRequest": "quiero que me ayudes a ponerle un login y que después la pueda probar en mi telefono",
  "description": "Signing in with Apple or Google, offered from the star menu and never required — El Carot stays fully usable without an account, which is the production default. An account adds two things: the home greeting uses your given name, and your daily cards move into a storage key scoped to that account, so signing out restores the signed-out reader's own trail untouched and a second person signing in on the same phone inherits nothing. All provider knowledge lives behind lib/auth.tsx, and the session-shaping rules are pure functions in lib/account.ts — including the one that matters most, that Apple returns a name only on the very first authorization, so a later sign-in must not blank out a name already known. Availability is exposed as data rather than as failure: Apple's button is iOS-only and Google's needs client ids from outside the repo, so each renders dimmed with the reason underneath instead of dying on tap. Three bugs surfaced along the way: ActionButton's disabled prop had never had any visual effect because opacity does not composite on this stack (pre-existing, and it was silently affecting the real question screen too); a four-part Spanish name overran the home header and collided with the language toggle and the star; and the seed injection writes declared keys without clearing undeclared ones, so once a persisted session existed any scenario omitting it inherited one from whichever capture ran before — fixed by pinning elcarot.session on every signed-out scenario.",
